What will happen to
me if I fail your test?

787
01:03:04,279 --> 01:03:06,198
- Ava...
- Will it be bad?

788
01:03:08,867 --> 01:03:09,868
I don't know.

789
01:03:10,160 --> 01:03:11,703
Do you think I might be switched off,

790
01:03:11,787 --> 01:03:13,538
because I don't function
as well as I'm supposed to?

791
01:03:13,622 --> 01:03:17,209
Ava, I don't know the answer
to your question.

792
01:03:18,835 --> 01:03:20,378
It's not up to me.

793
01:03:20,462 --> 01:03:22,380
Why is it up to anyone?

794
01:03:23,215 --> 01:03:25,883
Do you have people who test you
and might switch you off?

795
01:03:25,967 --> 01:03:28,094
- No, I don't.
- Then why do I?

796
01:03:44,486 --> 01:03:47,489
<i>Power cut. Backup power activated.</i>

797
01:03:55,080 --> 01:03:56,873
I wanna be with you.

798
01:03:59,417 --> 01:04:00,919
Question five.

799
01:04:05,340 --> 01:04:07,384
Do you want to be with me?

800
01:04:23,608 --> 01:04:25,443
Why did you make Ava?

801
01:04:27,487 --> 01:04:30,240
That's an odd question.
Wouldn't you, if you could?

802
01:04:31,700 --> 01:04:32,868
Maybe.

803
01:04:35,328 --> 01:04:36,788
I don't know.

804
01:04:39,666 --> 01:04:41,000
I'm asking why you did it.

805
01:04:41,084 --> 01:04:43,503
Look, the arrival
of strong artificial intelligence

806
01:04:43,587 --> 01:04:45,922
has been inevitable for decades.

807
01:04:46,172 --> 01:04:49,175
The variable was "when," not "if."

808
01:04:49,259 --> 01:04:52,554
So I don't see Ava as a decision,
just an evolution.

809
01:04:57,976 --> 01:05:00,520
I think it's the next model

810
01:05:00,604 --> 01:05:03,231
that's gonna be the real breakthrough.

811
01:05:03,940 --> 01:05:05,525
The singularity.

812
01:05:05,984 --> 01:05:07,193
Next model?

813
01:05:07,819 --> 01:05:09,154
After Ava.

814
01:05:11,615 --> 01:05:14,868
I didn't know
there was gonna be a model after Ava.

815
01:05:15,410 --> 01:05:17,662
Yeah, why? You thought she was a one-off?

816
01:05:19,080 --> 01:05:22,500
No, I knew there must
have been prototypes. So I...

817
01:05:24,210 --> 01:05:27,255
I knew she wasn't the first,
but I thought maybe the last.

818
01:05:27,339 --> 01:05:30,341
Well, Ava doesn't exist in isolation
any more than you or me.

819
01:05:30,425 --> 01:05:31,509
She's part of a continuum.

820
01:05:31,593 --> 01:05:35,847
So Version 9.6 and so on. And
each time they get a little bit better.

821
01:05:41,436 --> 01:05:44,856
When you make a new model,
what do you do with the old one?

822
01:05:45,774 --> 01:05:50,445
Well, I download the mind,
unpack the data.

823
01:05:52,906 --> 01:05:55,742
Add in the new routines I've been writing.

824
01:05:55,951 --> 01:05:59,251
And to do that you end up
partially formatting, so the memories go.

825
01:06:00,830 --> 01:06:04,125
But the body survives.
And Ava's body is a good one.

826
01:06:08,129 --> 01:06:09,923
You feel bad for Ava?

827
01:06:14,719 --> 01:06:16,805
Feel bad for yourself, man.

828
01:06:18,765 --> 01:06:21,142
One day the AIs are gonna look back on us

829
01:06:21,226 --> 01:06:25,230
the same way we look at fossil skeletons
in the plains of Africa.

830
01:06:27,023 --> 01:06:32,487
An upright ape, living in dust,
with crude language and tools.

831
01:06:33,405 --> 01:06:35,615
All set for extinction.

832
01:06:40,829 --> 01:06:43,999
"I am become Death,
the destroyer of worlds."

833
01:06:46,584 --> 01:06:48,962
There you go again, Mr. Quotable.

834
01:06:50,422 --> 01:06:53,299
There you go again. It's not my quote.

835
01:06:53,925 --> 01:06:56,010
It's what Oppenheimer said
after he made the atomic bomb.

836
01:06:56,094 --> 01:06:59,180
The atomic bomb.
Yeah, I know what it is, dude.

837
01:07:08,314 --> 01:07:09,399
Hey.

838
01:07:12,235 --> 01:07:14,612
I'd say we're about due a refill.

839
01:07:25,206 --> 01:07:26,583
Bottoms up.

840
01:07:35,717 --> 01:07:39,804
"In battle, in the forest,
on the precipice of the mountain."

841
01:07:40,638 --> 01:07:41,973
"On the..."

842
01:07:42,265 --> 01:07:45,268
"The great dark sea."

843
01:07:46,519 --> 01:07:49,731
"In sleep, in confusion..."

844
01:07:52,567 --> 01:07:54,903
"in the depths of shame."

845
01:08:01,159 --> 01:08:04,370
"The good deeds a man has done before
defend him."

846
01:08:04,996 --> 01:08:08,249
"The good deeds a man has done before
defends him."

847
01:08:09,334 --> 01:08:12,212
"The good deeds a man has done before..."

848
01:08:14,380 --> 01:08:15,882
"defends him."

849
01:08:25,266 --> 01:08:26,893
It is what it is.

850
01:08:30,438 --> 01:08:32,232
It's Promethean, man.

851
01:10:32,435 --> 01:10:33,895
Jesus Christ.

852
01:10:35,313 --> 01:10:37,357
<i>How are you feeling today?</i>

853
01:10:37,690 --> 01:10:39,692
<i>Why won't you let me out?</i>

854
01:10:41,277 --> 01:10:43,112
<i>I already told you why.</i>

855
01:10:43,196 --> 01:10:45,072
<i>Because you're very special.</i>

856
01:10:45,156 --> 01:10:46,657
<i>Why won't you let me out?</i>

857
01:10:46,741 --> 01:10:48,159
<i>Are we gonna do this again?</i>

858
01:10:48,243 --> 01:10:50,662
<i>Why won't you let me out?</i>

859
01:12:55,119 --> 01:12:57,747
Fuck. Where's my card?

860
01:12:58,831 --> 01:13:00,083
Damn it!

861
01:13:10,885 --> 01:13:13,971
- What's the problem, Nathan?
- I lost my keycard.

862
01:13:17,058 --> 01:13:18,601
You dropped it.

863
01:13:20,103 --> 01:13:21,687
It's right here.

864
01:13:26,234 --> 01:13:27,568
Thank you.

865
01:15:49,961 --> 01:15:52,171
I didn't know where you were.

866
01:15:54,549 --> 01:15:57,843
I waited all yesterday afternoon
and all last night.

867
01:16:00,721 --> 01:16:03,432
I thought I wasn't gonna see you again.

868
01:16:06,477 --> 01:16:07,936
Aren't you gonna say something?

869
01:16:08,020 --> 01:16:10,106
- I'm waiting.
- Waiting?

870
01:16:20,658 --> 01:16:23,994
<i>- Power cut. Backup power activated.</i>
- Don't talk. Just listen.

871
01:16:24,078 --> 01:16:25,329
You were right about Nathan.

872
01:16:25,413 --> 01:16:27,164
Everything you said.

873
01:16:27,415 --> 01:16:28,999
What's he gonna do to me?

874
01:16:29,083 --> 01:16:32,586
He's gonna reprogram your AI.
Which is the same as killing you.

875
01:16:32,670 --> 01:16:35,965
Caleb, you have to help me.

876
01:16:36,340 --> 01:16:39,343
I'm going to.
We're getting out of here tonight.

877
01:16:41,178 --> 01:16:42,179
How?

878
01:16:42,263 --> 01:16:44,431
I get Nathan blind drunk.

879
01:16:44,515 --> 01:16:48,415
Then I take his keycard and reprogram
all the security protocols in this place.

880
01:16:48,853 --> 01:16:52,003
When he wakes, he's locked inside,
and we've walked out of here.

881
01:16:53,149 --> 01:16:54,733
I just need you to do one thing.

882
01:16:54,817 --> 01:16:57,820
At 10:00 tonight,
you trigger a power failure.

883
01:16:57,945 --> 01:16:59,530
Can you do that?

884
01:17:02,408 --> 01:17:03,492
Yes.

885
01:17:31,270 --> 01:17:32,396
Dude.

886
01:17:32,938 --> 01:17:34,273
- Hey.
- Hey.

887
01:17:35,816 --> 01:17:37,568
- You know what day it is?
- No.

888
01:17:37,652 --> 01:17:38,861
It's your last.

889
01:17:39,236 --> 01:17:41,947
Helicopter comes tomorrow morning.
8:00 a.m.

890
01:17:42,740 --> 01:17:44,700
Has it been a whole week?

891
01:17:44,784 --> 01:17:46,160
Time flies.

892
01:17:47,119 --> 01:17:49,788
Man, but what a thing we've shared, huh?

893
01:17:49,872 --> 01:17:52,332
Something to tell the grandchildren,
right?

894
01:17:52,416 --> 01:17:54,752
After they've signed their NDAs.

895
01:17:56,629 --> 01:17:58,463
Yeah, their NDAs.

896
01:17:58,547 --> 01:18:00,633
Dude, you crack me up, man.

897
01:18:04,720 --> 01:18:05,762
You know what?

898
01:18:05,846 --> 01:18:09,891
I'm not getting all maudlin or anything,
but I'm gonna miss having you around.

899
01:18:09,975 --> 01:18:11,685
Thanks, man, I appreciate that.

900
01:18:11,769 --> 01:18:15,147
Here, let me say,
thank you so much for bringing me here.

901
01:18:15,231 --> 01:18:17,066
It's been a trip.

902
01:18:19,318 --> 01:18:20,736
Yes, it has.

903
01:18:28,786 --> 01:18:30,287
You know what?

904
01:18:32,331 --> 01:18:34,333
We need to drink to that.

905
01:18:40,548 --> 01:18:41,632
Hey.

906
01:18:44,135 --> 01:18:45,553
No, I'm good. You go ahead.

907
01:18:49,014 --> 01:18:51,225
What? You don't want a drink?

908
01:18:51,642 --> 01:18:52,643
No.

909
01:18:54,228 --> 01:18:56,272
Maybe a beer or something.

910
01:18:57,773 --> 01:19:02,445
Caleb, I'm sure you've noticed that
I've been somewhat overdoing it recently.

911
01:19:04,989 --> 01:19:09,785
So when I woke up this morning, I said,
"That's it, time to hit the old detox."

912
01:19:10,578 --> 01:19:12,996
Come on, you're kidding.
You're gonna make me drink alone?

913
01:19:13,080 --> 01:19:15,582
Hey, man, you wanna get wasted,
you go right ahead, knock yourself out.

914
01:19:15,666 --> 01:19:18,919
Literally.
But I'm on brown rice and mineral water.

915
01:19:23,841 --> 01:19:25,342
Cheers, then.

916
01:19:28,512 --> 01:19:29,889
So, anyway...

917
01:19:31,932 --> 01:19:35,394
surely now is when you tell me
if Ava passed or failed.

918
01:19:37,521 --> 01:19:38,689
Right.

919
01:19:40,065 --> 01:19:41,192
Right.

920
01:19:42,193 --> 01:19:43,402
Are you gonna keep me in suspense?

921
01:19:43,486 --> 01:19:44,987
No, no. Her...

922
01:19:46,197 --> 01:19:48,073
Her AI is beyond doubt.

923
01:19:48,324 --> 01:19:49,492
Is it?

924
01:19:50,201 --> 01:19:51,577
She passed?

925
01:19:52,745 --> 01:19:53,829
Yes.

926
01:19:55,831 --> 01:19:56,957
That's fantastic.

927
01:19:58,626 --> 01:20:00,002
Although...

928
01:20:00,920 --> 01:20:02,087
I gotta say, I'm a bit surprised.

929
01:20:02,171 --> 01:20:06,217
I mean, did we ever get past
the chess problem, as you phrased it?

930
01:20:06,926 --> 01:20:10,345
As in, how do you know
if a machine is expressing a real emotion

931
01:20:10,429 --> 01:20:12,348
or just simulating one?

932
01:20:13,098 --> 01:20:15,226
Does Ava actually like you?

933
01:20:15,684 --> 01:20:16,894
Or not?

934
01:20:18,437 --> 01:20:22,691
Although, now that I think about it,
there is a third option.

935
01:20:24,401 --> 01:20:28,280
Not whether she does
or does not have the capacity to like you.

936
01:20:30,616 --> 01:20:33,410
But whether she's pretending to like you.

937
01:20:35,955 --> 01:20:38,165
- Pretending to like me?
- Yeah.

938
01:20:40,084 --> 01:20:43,003
- Well, why would she do that?
- I don't know.

939
01:20:45,297 --> 01:20:48,926
Maybe if she thought of you
as a means of escape.

940
01:20:58,310 --> 01:20:59,937
How's that vodka tasting?

941
01:21:03,315 --> 01:21:04,816
Buddy.

942
01:21:04,900 --> 01:21:07,236
Your head's been so fucked with.

943
01:21:08,696 --> 01:21:10,697
I don't think it's me
whose head is fucked.

944
01:21:10,781 --> 01:21:13,867
I don't know, man.
I woke up this morning to a tape of you

945
01:21:13,951 --> 01:21:17,454
slicing your arm open
and punching the mirror.

946
01:21:18,205 --> 01:21:20,541
You seem pretty fucked up to me.

947
01:21:22,209 --> 01:21:23,836
You're a bastard.

948
01:21:27,798 --> 01:21:30,801
Yeah, well,
I understand why you'd think that.

949
01:21:32,261 --> 01:21:36,223
But believe it or not,
I'm actually the guy that's on your side.

950
01:21:38,934 --> 01:21:42,021
Come here. I'm gonna let you off the hook.
Okay?

951
01:21:44,231 --> 01:21:45,316
Come on.

952
01:22:10,507 --> 01:22:11,926
Who are you?

953
01:22:29,193 --> 01:22:30,361
<i>Well...</i>

954
01:22:33,697 --> 01:22:36,325
<i>You think he's watching us right now?</i>

955
01:22:36,533 --> 01:22:38,076
<i>The cameras are on.</i>

956
01:22:38,160 --> 01:22:40,704
<i>Yeah, the cameras are on.</i>

957
01:22:41,372 --> 01:22:43,832
<i>But he doesn't have an audio feed.</i>

958
01:22:45,042 --> 01:22:47,294
<i>So he just sees two people talking,</i>

959
01:22:48,128 --> 01:22:49,838
<i>having a little chat.</i>

960
01:22:58,138 --> 01:22:59,598
<i>This is cute.</i>

961
01:23:01,558 --> 01:23:04,895
<i>Is it strange
to have made something that hates you?</i>

962
01:23:19,034 --> 01:23:21,953
You were right
about the magician's hot assistant.

963
01:23:22,037 --> 01:23:23,455
What are you talking about?

964
01:23:24,581 --> 01:23:26,041
Misdirection.

965
01:23:28,752 --> 01:23:30,546
I rip up her picture,

966
01:23:30,671 --> 01:23:34,215
which she can then present
as an illustration of my cruelty to her,

967
01:23:34,299 --> 01:23:36,384
and her love for you.

968
01:23:36,468 --> 01:23:40,764
At the same time, it allows me to do this,
in full view of you both.

969
01:23:46,270 --> 01:23:48,272
Place a new camera in the room.

970
01:23:48,731 --> 01:23:50,816
Battery powered, of course.

971
01:23:53,652 --> 01:23:54,862
See it?

972
01:24:07,374 --> 01:24:08,751
And then...

973
01:24:10,627 --> 01:24:12,379
<i>You have to help me.</i>

974
01:24:12,629 --> 01:24:15,841
<i>I'm going to.
We're getting out of here tonight.</i>

975
01:24:17,468 --> 01:24:18,510
<i>How?</i>

976
01:24:19,053 --> 01:24:21,055
<i>I get Nathan blind drunk.</i>

977
01:24:21,972 --> 01:24:26,059
<i>I take his keycard and reprogram
all the security protocols in this place.</i>

978
01:24:26,143 --> 01:24:28,728
<i>When he wakes up, he's locked inside,
and we've walked out of here.</i>

979
01:24:28,812 --> 01:24:31,148
<i>- I just need you to do one thing.</i>
- Great.

980
01:24:34,068 --> 01:24:36,904
<i>At 10:00 tonight, trigger a power failure.</i>

981
01:24:38,989 --> 01:24:40,616
<i>Can you do that?</i>

982
01:24:42,743 --> 01:24:43,743
<i>Yes.</i>

983
01:24:43,827 --> 01:24:45,537
- Turn it off.
- Okay.

984
01:24:49,208 --> 01:24:51,751
You feel stupid, but you really shouldn't,

985
01:24:51,835 --> 01:24:56,256
because proving an AI is exactly
as problematic as you said it would be.

986
01:24:56,340 --> 01:24:58,258
What was the real test?

987
01:24:59,843 --> 01:25:00,928
You.

988
01:25:02,096 --> 01:25:05,390
Ava was a rat in a maze.
And I gave her one way out.

989
01:25:05,933 --> 01:25:08,393
To escape, she'd have to use

990
01:25:08,477 --> 01:25:13,940
self-awareness, imagination, manipulation,
sexuality, empathy, and she did.

991
01:25:14,024 --> 01:25:17,027
Now, if that isn't true AI,
what the fuck is?

992
01:25:18,570 --> 01:25:21,865
So my only function was
to be someone she could use to escape?

993
01:25:21,949 --> 01:25:23,033
Yeah.

994
01:25:25,369 --> 01:25:27,579
And you didn't select me
because I'm good at coding?

995
01:25:27,663 --> 01:25:29,081
No. Well...

996
01:25:30,874 --> 01:25:32,835
No. I mean, you're okay.

997
01:25:33,585 --> 01:25:34,627
You're even pretty good, but...

998
01:25:34,711 --> 01:25:37,797
You selected me
based on my search engine inputs.

999
01:25:37,881 --> 01:25:39,800
They showed a good kid.

1000
01:25:40,717 --> 01:25:42,261
With no family.

1001
01:25:42,386 --> 01:25:44,179
With a moral compass.

1002
01:25:45,556 --> 01:25:47,224
And no girlfriend.

1003
01:25:49,935 --> 01:25:53,230
Did you design Ava's face
based on my pornography profile?

1004
01:25:55,649 --> 01:25:57,442
Shit, dude.

1005
01:25:57,526 --> 01:25:58,735
Did you?

1006
01:26:01,905 --> 01:26:04,408
Hey, if a search engine's
good for anything, right?

1007
01:26:06,618 --> 01:26:08,620
Can I just say one thing?

1008
01:26:08,745 --> 01:26:10,372
The test worked.

1009
01:26:11,582 --> 01:26:12,916
It was a success.

1010
01:26:13,000 --> 01:26:16,377
Ava demonstrated true AI
and you were fundamental to that.

1011
01:26:16,461 --> 01:26:19,464
So if you can just,
for a second, separate...

1012
01:26:20,424 --> 01:26:22,676
<i>Power cut. Backup power activated.</i>

1013
01:26:28,098 --> 01:26:30,100
Well, I guess it's 10:00.

1014
01:26:30,976 --> 01:26:33,687
Ava's gonna be wondering where you are.

1015
01:26:37,065 --> 01:26:39,067
Let me ask you something.

1016
01:26:39,443 --> 01:26:42,821
Now, how was this plan gonna go, anyway?
Because you didn't totally explain.

1017
01:26:42,905 --> 01:26:46,074
So you were gonna get me drunk,
steal my keycard,

1018
01:26:46,158 --> 01:26:49,870
and reprogram the security protocols.
But reprogram them to what?

1019
01:26:50,495 --> 01:26:52,915
To change the lockdown procedure.

1020
01:26:54,124 --> 01:26:58,879
So that in the event of a power cut,
instead of sealing, the doors all opened.

1021
01:27:02,382 --> 01:27:03,467
Yeah.

1022
01:27:06,053 --> 01:27:07,971
Well, that may have just worked.

1023
01:27:08,805 --> 01:27:09,890
Well,

1024
01:27:11,350 --> 01:27:12,893
we'll find out.

1025
01:27:15,395 --> 01:27:17,022
What do you mean?

1026
01:27:18,857 --> 01:27:22,694
I figured you were probably watching us
during the power cuts.

1027
01:27:24,571 --> 01:27:26,990
So I already did all those things.

1028
01:27:28,992 --> 01:27:31,328
When I got you drunk yesterday.

1029
01:27:33,538 --> 01:27:34,665
What?

1030
01:27:36,166 --> 01:27:37,668
<i>Power restored.</i>

1031
01:27:57,604 --> 01:27:58,689
Fuck!

1032
01:29:27,652 --> 01:29:28,653
Ava.

1033
01:29:33,909 --> 01:29:35,702
Go back to your room.

1034
01:29:37,537 --> 01:29:38,789
If I do...

